{
  "root_cause": "config_change",
  "summary": "A configuration change to the 'strict_session_binding' flag was rolled out from 5% to 100% at 09:17, which caused a large spike in session re-authentication and 401 errors due to session invalidation. This led to increased error rates and forced re-auth warnings in the API service, causing the incident.",
  "onset_ts": "2026-03-17T09:18:00.000Z",
  "timeline": [
    {
      "statement": "At 09:17, the 'strict_session_binding' flag rollout was increased from 5% to 100%, which was unintended.",
      "citations": [
        {
          "source": "changes.jsonl",
          "line": 1,
          "quote": "\"rollout 5% -> 100% (intended 5%)\""
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "At 09:18, the re-authentication rate spiked dramatically from 9-15 per minute to 285 per minute, indicating many forced re-auths.",
      "citations": [
        {
          "source": "metrics/auth.csv",
          "line": 20,
          "quote": "2026-03-17T09:18:00.000Z,8524,285"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "At 09:18, the API error rate jumped sharply from ~0.0025 to 0.052, reflecting many 401 unauthorized errors.",
      "citations": [
        {
          "source": "metrics/http.csv",
          "line": 20,
          "quote": "2026-03-17T09:18:00.000Z,46,177.27,0.052,348"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Warnings about 'session binding mismatch, forcing re-auth' started appearing at 09:18 and continued throughout the incident.",
      "citations": [
        {
          "source": "logs/app.jsonl",
          "line": 533,
          "quote": "\"session binding mismatch, forcing re-auth\""
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Errors of 'request rejected: session invalid' also started at 09:18 and persisted, confirming session invalidation issues.",
      "citations": [
        {
          "source": "logs/app.jsonl",
          "line": 535,
          "quote": "\"request rejected: session invalid\""
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "An autoscaler increased API replicas from 6 to 9 at 09:40 in response to the increased load.",
      "citations": [
        {
          "source": "changes.jsonl",
          "line": 2,
          "quote": "\"api replicas 6 -> 9\""
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Alerts for 'AuthReauthSpike' and 'Api401RateHigh' fired at 09:24 and 09:26 respectively, indicating recognition of the problem.",
      "citations": [
        {
          "source": "alerts.jsonl",
          "line": 1,
          "quote": "\"AuthReauthSpike\",\"state\":\"firing\""
        },
        {
          "source": "alerts.jsonl",
          "line": 2,
          "quote": "\"Api401RateHigh\",\"state\":\"firing\""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "evidence": [
    {
      "statement": "The timing of the flag rollout at 09:17 directly precedes the spike in re-authentication and 401 errors starting at 09:18.",
      "citations": [
        {
          "source": "changes.jsonl",
          "line": 1,
          "quote": "\"rollout 5% -> 100% (intended 5%)\""
        },
        {
          "source": "metrics/auth.csv",
          "line": 20,
          "quote": "2026-03-17T09:18:00.000Z,8524,285"
        },
        {
          "source": "metrics/http.csv",
          "line": 20,
          "quote": "2026-03-17T09:18:00.000Z,46,177.27,0.052,348"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Logs show repeated warnings and errors about session binding mismatches and invalid sessions, consistent with the strict session binding flag causing forced re-authentication.",
      "citations": [
        {
          "source": "logs/app.jsonl",
          "line": 533,
          "quote": "\"session binding mismatch, forcing re-auth\""
        },
        {
          "source": "logs/app.jsonl",
          "line": 535,
          "quote": "\"request rejected: session invalid\""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "ruled_out": [
    {
      "statement": "Resource exhaustion or memory leak is unlikely because the API replicas were scaled up at 09:40, but the error rate and re-auth spikes started much earlier at 09:18.",
      "citations": [
        {
          "source": "changes.jsonl",
          "line": 2,
          "quote": "\"api replicas 6 -> 9\""
        },
        {
          "source": "metrics/auth.csv",
          "line": 20,
          "quote": "2026-03-17T09:18:00.000Z,8524,285"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Downstream dependency failure is not supported by the data, as the errors are specifically 401 unauthorized due to session invalidation, not timeouts or 5xx errors.",
      "citations": [
        {
          "source": "logs/app.jsonl",
          "line": 535,
          "quote": "\"request rejected: session invalid\""
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "No evidence of DNS failure, certificate expiry, or schema migration regression was found in logs or metrics.",
      "citations": []
    }
  ],
  "action_items": [
    "Implement stricter rollout controls and verification for feature flags to prevent unintended full rollouts.",
    "Add automated monitoring to detect sudden spikes in re-authentication rates immediately after config changes.",
    "Improve rollback procedures to quickly revert problematic config changes.",
    "Review and update documentation and training for flag rollout processes."
  ]
}
